Z||000000||spideyfoot||04-15-2001||11:56 AM||||hey guys does anyone know a good trick for covering/removing the webby looking cracks before I paint I've been able to sand through most but some are in the yellow. Also Ive hit bare glass in my hood(removing old bubbles) is the trick to just put a thin layer of bondo over to smooth out. <BR>Thanks Spideyfoot<BR>88 4 banging 5 stick||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||04-15-2001||01:32 PM||||In hard panels like the hood you'll have to clean them out and fill them. In the nose and tail.... good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowfunds||04-15-2001||02:16 PM||||I have been able to repare the front clip with a thin layer of bondo. But I would feel better using flexable bumper filler. Its a bondo for flexable panels.(expensive though)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||04-15-2001||02:40 PM||||me & my brother used spot filler for mine when we did em last time, filled in nicely<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GoCartGuy||04-15-2001||08:22 PM||||For the front use Napa's flex bumper repair kit.  Cost me like $25, I used it to fix a broken dash corner and the plastic surrounds for the instrument cluster and center panel.  Anyways its good stuff and seems to go a long way.  Well worth the $25 since I also used it for some other patches around the house.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||jch82||04-16-2001||12:36 AM||||Yup, the flexible bumper repair is the way to go! Make sure you get all the spiderwebs out before you paint, otherwise the paint wont stick to the cracks....<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||12
